---
import Ladder from "../components/Ladder.astro";
import Schedule from "../components/Schedule.astro";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
---

<PageLayout title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`} description={courseMeta.description} lead={false}>
  <div class="kicker">
    {courseMeta.code} · Postgraduate · {courseMeta.session}, {courseMeta.year}
  </div>
  <ul class="tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <h1>{courseMeta.title}</h1>
  <hr class="rule" />
  <p class="lede">
    Every other treatment has to beat a placebo. Surgery mostly doesn't. This
    course spends twelve weeks on the operation that makes the comparison
    possible: the one where nothing is done, carefully.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    A sham procedure is not the absence of an operation. It is an operation —
    designed, rehearsed, consented and reviewed — whose only job is to leave
    the real one nothing to hide behind.
  </blockquote>

  <figure>
    <Ladder />
    <figcaption>
      <strong>The Sham Fidelity Ladder.</strong> Introduced in Round 4, used in
      every Round after it. Every rung up buys blinding with risk. Round 7 is
      about who is allowed to make that purchase.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="two">
    <div>
      <h2>What you will make</h2>
      <p>
        By Week 12 you will have written a complete sham-controlled protocol
        for a procedure that is performed today without one. You build it one
        section per Round. Nobody is operated on. The protocol is the
        operation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Surgical trainees, trial methodologists, perioperative and research
        nurses, biostatisticians, ethicists, and anyone who has said "well, it
        obviously works" about a procedure and would like to find out whether
        that is true.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Five trials you will know by heart</h2>
  <ul class="trials">
    <li>Moseley et al., 2002 — arthroscopic surgery for knee osteoarthritis</li>
    <li>
      Buchbinder et al. and Kallmes et al., 2009 — vertebroplasty for
      osteoporotic fractures
    </li>
    <li>ORBITA (Al-Lamee et al.), 2017 — PCI for stable angina</li>
    <li>
      SYMPLICITY HTN-3 (Bhatt et al.), 2014 — renal denervation for resistant
      hypertension
    </li>
    <li>
      Freed et al., 2001 — embryonic dopamine-neuron transplantation for
      Parkinson's disease
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Schedule />

  <p class="foot">No patients will be operated on in this course, sham or otherwise.</p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .kicker {
    color: var(--sham-drape);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
  }

  .tags li {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--sham-drape);
    background: var(--sham-drape-tint);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.65rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .rule {
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--sham-incision);
    width: 7.5rem;
    margin: 1.1rem 0 1.25rem;
    border: 0;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.35rem;
    border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--sham-drape);
    background: var(--sham-drape-tint);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  figure picture {
    display: block;
  }

  figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 45rem;
    display: block;
  }

  figcaption {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary, #4a5a55);
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  .two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .trials {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .trials li {
    margin: 0.25rem 0;
  }

  .foot {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary, #4a5a55);
    margin-block-start: 2.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .two {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
